Open CASCADE Technology
=============================================================================

This software makes use of facilities provided by the Open CASCADE
Technology software (https://dev.opencascade.org).

stepv's kernel (the `stepv-occt` program and the `libstepvocct` library) is
built on Open CASCADE Technology (OCCT) 7.9.3, which is licensed under the
GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 with the Open CASCADE
exception version 1.0:

  licenses/OCCT-LGPL-2.1.txt
  licenses/OCCT-LGPL-EXCEPTION-1.0.txt

Corresponding source: https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/tree/V7_9_3,
as packaged by nixpkgs, with the one modification below.

Modification. The OCCT that stepv's packages ship (and that its nix build
links against) is built with one patch, to one file:

  file:    src/ShapeFix/ShapeFix_IntersectionTool.cxx (library TKShHealing)
  patch:   nix/patches/occt-7.9.3-fixselfintersectwire-hoist.patch, a
           path from the root of stepv's source archive for this release
           (https://github.com/vig-os/stepv/releases, the tag of this
           package's version); flake.nix applies it
  what:    ShapeFix_IntersectionTool::FixSelfIntersectWire() fetches the
           outer loop's edge once per outer iteration (and again after the
           branch that removes it), instead of on every inner iteration.
           The result is unchanged; healing a wire of n edges takes O(n^2)
           time instead of O(n^3) (stepv#74).
  licence: the modified file stays under OCCT's licence, the LGPL 2.1 with
           the Open CASCADE exception 1.0 above, and carries a notice of the
           change and its date.

The corresponding source of the shipped OCCT is the V7_9_3 tree above plus
that patch.

stepv's kernel/heal.cpp follows OCCT's own fixshape() operator
(ShapeProcess_OperLibrary.cxx, under the licence above): it reads the same
healing parameters, with the same defaults, runs the same passes and records
their history the same way, and adds a time budget on fixing each face. It is
stepv's own code, registered through OCCT's public ShapeProcess API; no OCCT
source file is copied into stepv's kernel.

OCCT is always DYNAMICALLY linked and kept in separate, replaceable files —
never compiled into the `stepv` binary:

  - Linux tarball: the OCCT shared libraries are stepv/lib/libTK*.so.
    Replace them with a build of the same OCCT version, patched or not.
  - macOS stepv.app: Contents/Frameworks/libTK*.dylib. Replace them with a
    build of the same OCCT version, patched or not, then re-sign the bundle
    (`codesign --force --deep --sign - stepv.app` for local use).
  - Building from source (crates.io, or this repository): you supply OCCT
    yourself (`cmake -S kernel -B build`); nothing of OCCT is distributed.
    An unpatched OCCT works; it heals long self-intersecting wires slowly.

